        "x1": 0.7931535947712419,
        "y1": 0.46329671717171717
      },
      "text": "We put ellipsoids Dj′ of the standard form one after another to have our desired result.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20706045751633986,
        "y0": 0.47950505050505043,
        "x1": 0.7930424836601307,
        "y1": 0.5228573232323233
      },
      "text": "Proposition 1. In the present inductive procedure, for a step putting an ellipsoid Dj′ centered at the point xj′ := (π2,1,1(v) ± ǫv,±,j,av,±,j) or xj′ := (π2,1,1(v0) ± ǫv",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.22019934640522876,
        "y0": 0.5098080808080807,
        "x1": 0.2735669934640523,
        "y1": 0.5238446969696969
      },
      "text": "0,±,j,av",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2264722222222222,
        "y0": 0.5098080808080807,
        "x1": 0.7855735294117647,
        "y1": 0.5525391414141414
      },
      "text": "0,±,j), we abuse the notation from Deﬁnition 4. First, Dj′ is (S,DS)-connected. In addition, we assume at least one of the following in a step in the procedure.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2472565359477124,
        "y0": 0.5598080808080808,
        "x1": 0.7377352941176472,
        "y1": 0.5732626262626263
      },
      "text": "• At least one ellipsoid centered at a point of the form (π2,1,1(v)±ǫv,±,j 0 ,av,±,j 0 ) has been put in the case v is of degree at least 3.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "list",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.24725816993464053,
        "y0": 0.589959595959596,
        "x1": 0.7208235294117648,
        "y1": 0.6034141414141414
      },
      "text": "• At least one ellipsoid centered at a point of the form (π2,1,1(v0)±ǫv",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2635326797385621,
        "y0": 0.589959595959596,
        "x1": 0.8229869281045752,
        "y1": 0.6185643939393939
      },
      "text": "0,±,j0) has been put in the case v0 is of degree 1.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7207875816993464,
        "y0": 0.589959595959596,
        "x1": 0.7800392156862745,
        "y1": 0.6039962121212121
      },
      "text": "0,±,j0,av",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20706045751633986,
        "y0": 0.6249595959595959,
        "x1": 0.7928758169934641,
        "y1": 0.6535656565656566
      },
      "text": ")-PLS and it is not (S,DS,AD",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2264722222222222,
        "y0": 0.6249595959595959,
        "x1": 0.7412336601307189,
        "y1": 0.6384141414141414
      },
      "text": "Under this additional assumption, the pointed set (Dj,xj′) is (S,DS,AD",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7411781045751634,
        "y0": 0.6327070707070707,
        "x1": 0.7482434640522876,
        "y1": 0.638996212121212
      },
      "text": "S",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3880408496732026,
        "y0": 0.6401111111111111,
        "x1": 0.42537418300653596,
        "y1": 0.6526906565656565
      },
      "text": ")-PS.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3788251633986928,
        "y0": 0.6478585858585859,
        "x1": 0.3858888888888889,
        "y1": 0.6541477272727272
      },
      "text": "S",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20705882352941177,
        "y0": 0.6651111111111111,
        "x1": 0.7930686274509804,
        "y1": 0.7088686868686869
      },
      "text": "Proof. The ﬁrst part follows from assumptions on a suﬃciently small positive number ǫ0 > 0, another suﬃciently small one ǫ > 0, and suﬃciently small ones with the relations 0 < ǫv,−,j,ǫv,+,j,ǫv",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20705882352941177,
        "y0": 0.6935479797979798,
        "x1": 0.7930408496732027,
        "y1": 0.7554330808080808
      },
      "text": "0,+,j < ǫ′ < ǫ. We see the additional part. The set Dj′ contains a point of the boundary Dj′ − Dj′ such that the value of the projection π2,1,1 there is π2,1,1(v) or π2,1,1(v0). The set Dj′ contains no point from FD",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.40705882352941175,
        "y0": 0.6954141414141415,
        "x1": 0.4584673202614379,
        "y1": 0.7094507575757576
      },
      "text": "0,−,j,ǫv",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.48449019607843136,
        "y0": 0.7100151515151515,
        "x1": 0.5093921568627451,
        "y1": 0.7106212121212121
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7525294117647059,
        "y0": 0.7100151515151515,
        "x1": 0.7774313725490196,
        "y1": 0.7106212121212121
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2333137254901961,
        "y0": 0.7410757575757576,
        "x1": 0.2582156862745098,
        "y1": 0.7416818181818181
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "caption",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20705882352941177,
        "y0": 0.7423838383838384,
        "x1": 0.7931078431372549,
        "y1": 0.770989898989899
      },
      "text": "S,2 by considering the local shape of the curve S0,c",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20705718954248364,
        "y0": 0.7575353535353535,
        "x1": 0.792983660130719,
        "y1": 0.8007361111111111
      },
      "text": ". From the additional assumption, there exists at least one point diﬀerent from this such that the value of the projection π2,1,1 there is π2,1,1(v) or π2,1,1(v0) in FD",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.23333333333333336,
        "y0": 0.7654962121212121,
        "x1": 0.24199346405228758,
        "y1": 0.7712891414141414
      },
      "text": "G",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20705882352941177,
        "y0": 0.7876868686868688,
        "x1": 0.7931519607843137,
        "y1": 0.8161401515151515
      },
      "text": ")-PLS and it is not (S,DS,AD",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2476454248366013,
        "y0": 0.7876868686868688,
        "x1": 0.7416225490196078,
        "y1": 0.8017234848484849
      },
      "text": "S,1. We can easily check that the pointed set (Dj,xj′) is (S,DS,AD",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7415686274509804,
        "y0": 0.7954343434343434,
        "x1": 0.7486323529411765,
        "y1": 0.8017234848484849
      },
      "text": "S",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.22647058823529412,
        "y0": 0.8026868686868687,
        "x1": 0.5615669934640523,
        "y1": 0.8440542929292929
      },
      "text": ")-PS. We present another example as our new result.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3780392156862745,
        "y0": 0.8104343434343435,
        "x1": 0.3851045751633987,
        "y1": 0.8167247474747474
      },
      "text": "S",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20705882352941177,
        "y0": 0.8566262626262626,
        "x1": 0.7930408496732027,
        "y1": 0.8852310606060606
      },
      "text": "Theorem 5. We also abuse the notation from Deﬁnition 4 here. In our steps here, for each pair of ellipsoids of the standard form centered at (π2,1,1(v0) −",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
